{{Unobtainable}}
'''Capsule Cat''' is a [[:Category:Special Cats|Special Cat]] that was obtainable as a [[Daily Bonus]] during the [[MattShea Collaboration Event]]. It was added in [[Version 1.5 Update|Version 1.5]]. In [[The Battle Cats Unite!]], it can be unlocked by clearing a stage with only one [[Cat Units|Cat Unit]].

{{Cat Info
|ID = 28
|rarity = EX
|name1 = Capsule Cat
|name2 = Cramped Cats
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Cramped Cats''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
<tabber>
Mobile=
Though very weak, this Cat can be used as an expendable one-shot bullet to smack an enemy in the face or kill a pesky peon in the way. It is very situational, and in many cases not very useful due to having one of the lowest health stats in the game.

Once [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev Cat]] is unlocked, this cat becomes little more than a placeholder, but can still be a fun toy to play with on easier stages. This unit can also be a budget Maglev when playing {{4c}} stages provided you have nothing better. It can be used to chip off damage without pushing too far, or to hit a wave attacker and then get killed by a peon so the wave attacker misses. However, this inevitably gets outclassed once you unlock [[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Stone Cat]], as it serves the same purpose, but it can actually survive and hold the line.

This Cat can also help for speedrunning some stages, which can help for [[Timed Score Reward]]s, such as the stages in [[Into the Future]]. He can also be used for starting certain enemies' attack animations, such as [[THE SLOTH]] or [[Director Kurosawah]], though again, [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev Cat]] and Stone Cat can do the same respectively, but better. If you have these two units, this unit may as well be a novelty and fodder for your [[User Rank]] thanks to its low cost to upgrade.
|-|
Nintendo Switch=
Capsule Cat becomes an essential unit when it comes to grinding Battle Items, Cat Tickets, and Rare Tickets. Due to its top-notch speed and potent attack power, Capsule Cat can swiftly eliminate early stages, such as Korea in the Empire of Cats, which can allow players to activate Catnip Chance sooner and net rewards quicker.
<br>
Typical farming strategies require the use of setting the Nintendo Switch console on tabletop mode, having both Joy Cons removed for Co-Op play, and then proceeding to use the touch screen to play a stage. Since Co-Op has each player get their own wallet and cash flow, you can instantaneously deploy the unit with another rusher (favorably with Maglev Cat as it and Capsule Cat have the highest speed and lowest costs for rushing) and swiftly beating the stage. Since the Nintendo Switch port also contains Cat Food bonuses for duplicate treasures (though limited to 50 duplicates), a player can use Capsule Cat in tandem with other low cost rushers.
</tabber>
{{Job|Classification = User Rank Dump & Rusher}}

